%S A395910 21,145,497,1205,2405,4153,6589,9909,14185,19537,25973,33729,43009,
%T A395910 53733,66181,80385,96329,114501,134673,157265,181925,209357,239193,
%U A395910 271973,307501,346105,387433,432245,480005,531769,586637,645645,707857,774177,844789,919201
%N A395910 Number of integer lattice points on or strictly inside a 3-dimensional horn torus with major radius n and minor radius n: (sqrt(x^2 + y^2) - n)^2 + z^2 <= n^2.
%C A395910 Number of points (x, y, z) in Z^3 satisfying (sqrt(x^2 + y^2) - n)^2 + z^2 <= n^2.
%C A395910 The continuous volume of this horn torus is 2 * Pi^2 * n^3. As n -> infinity, a(n) / (2 * Pi^2 * n^3) -> 1.
%C A395910 Horizontal cross sections at height z are circular annuli bounded by (n - sqrt(n^2 - z^2))^2 <= x^2 + y^2 <= (n + sqrt(n^2 - z^2))^2. At z = 0, the inner hole closes to a single point, forming a full disk of radius 2*n.
%H A395910 Andrew J. Morris, <a href="/A395910/b395910.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A395910 Andrew J. Morris, <a href="/A395910/a395910.txt">C++ program</a>
%H A395910 Andrew J. Morris, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22282210">An Integer-Only Orthotropic Lattice Enumeration Framework and Asymptotic Convergence of Discrete Rational Pi</a>, Zenodo Preprint (2026).
%H A395910 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HornTorus.html">Horn Torus</a>
%F A395910 a(n) = A057655(4*n^2) + 2 * Sum_{z=1..n} N(n, z), where N(n, z) = A057655(floor((n + sqrt(n^2 - z^2))^2)) - A057655(ceiling((n - sqrt(n^2 - z^2))^2) - 1).
%e A395910 For n = 1:
%e A395910 Slice z = 0: x^2 + y^2 <= 4 contains 13 points: (0,0), (+-1,0), (0,+-1), (+-1,+-1), (+-2,0), (0,+-2).
%e A395910 Slice z = 1: x^2 + y^2 = 1 contains 4 points: (+-1,0), (0,+-1).
%e A395910 Slice z = -1: x^2 + y^2 = 1 contains 4 points: (+-1,0), (0,+-1).
%e A395910 Total a(1) = 13 + 4 + 4 = 21.
%o A395910 (C++) // See links
%Y A395910 Cf. A057655 (number of points in circle of squared radius n: x^2 + y^2 <= n).
%Y A395910 Cf. A000328 (number of points in circle of radius n: x^2 + y^2 <= n^2).
%K A395910 nonn,easy,new
%O A395910 1,1
